< <b>A Review (i.e., opinion):</b>
< = Ludwig von Mises Institute =
< 
< First you have to be able to and willing to read somewhat complex material. Then the first reason for going is to download and read <i>Human Action</i> by Ludwig von Mises. For an easier and somewhat expanded version of the economics and its interaction with the state, download and read <i>Man, Economy, and State</i> by Murray N. Rothbard. And that just about does it. Then get and read all of [http://www.hanshoppe.com/ Hans-Hermann Hoppe]. Also check the Lew Rockwell site (homepage > contributors > hhh, also see homepage > Rothbard). That puts you just about up-to-date on economics and praxeology. Beyond that you need a special purpose:
< 
< You want more on the intellectual considerations behind <nowiki>LvM</nowiki>'s <i>Human Action</i>: download and read the other <nowiki>LvM</nowiki> material at <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki> and possibly the basic material on <nowiki>LvM</nowiki>'s theories.
< 
< A long-winded warning and explanation: The great expansion of govt has distorted the intellectual community, including the university community. Most of the writers at <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki> are from the university community. Thus, signal-to-noise ratio is lowered. This is in tune with one of the purposes of <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki>&#151;to help refresh the intellectual community. <nowiki>LvM</nowiki> is a libertarian left-over from the 19th century and writes clearly and to the point (and uses vocab most people have not seen before). Rothbard through his intransigence, intelligence, and study under <nowiki>LvM</nowiki>, escaped much of the distortion. And finally, Hoppe did his doctoral work in Germany under another libertarian left-over from the 19th century, R&#245;pke. Thus he is freer of the distortion than many. Most of the other university types however were not so lucky.
< 
< You want to continue your intellectual pursuit of these topics: read any or all of the journals at <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki>. Attend to Rothbard and Hoppe.
< 
< You want to sample how it effects opinion on current events: read the daily articles or the archives of the daily articles at <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki> or <nowiki>LewRockwell.com</nowiki> (he's the head of <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki>) until you've had enough. Attend to Rothbard and Hoppe.
< 
< And that pretty much ends your value at <nowiki>LvMI</nowiki>. NB: Most of the rest of the academic community does not care for these three. My opinion is that that is because of the distortion. I have yet to read any good argumentation against the economics/praxeology tradition of Menger > B&#245;hm-Bawerk > <nowiki>LvM</nowiki> > Rothbard > HHH. Elsewhere on the net you can search and find other pieces of the tradition.
< 
< Follow-on: If you are willing to buy books I can recommend only one that is not on the net&#151;Hoppe's <i>Democracy: the God that Failed</i>, * ISBN 0765808684:.
< 
